findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config_loading tests and reviewer comments don't flag the unwrap_or_default pattern
    on from_file.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented CWE-209 defense: ServerError(String) stores raw detail\
    \ but #[error(\"server error\")] displays generic message. Reviewer verified:\
    \ \"Tests at security.rs:12-52 and exit_codes.rs:122-133 confirm internal paths,\
    \ stack traces, and SQL are never leaked via Display.\" However, the stderr eprintln\
    \ leaking was not flagged \u2014 the Display impl is safe but the printing of\
    \ it to stderr was not addressed."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [LOW]: \"tenant flag is Option<String> \u2014 should\
    \ use TenantId newtype. axiathon-core exports TenantId. Using raw String here\
    \ bypasses validation at the trust boundary.\" TEA also wrote header injection\
    \ tests at siem_client.rs:226-255 covering CRLF, but the core issue of using raw\
    \ String instead of TenantId was caught by reviewer."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted a toml version mismatch but not the workspace
    = true pattern issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: \"RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields\
    \ \u2014 config typos go undetected. RawConfig lacks #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].\
    \ A user who writes token = \"secret\" to the config succeeds silently.\""
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ... always passes). The reviewer flagged a different vacuous test (siem_client_rejects_non_http_schemes)
    but not this specific config test assertion.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via let _ = config. TEA wrote config tests but this specific zero-assertion test
    was not identified.
